  "title": "Dual Adversarial Fine-tuning for Enhancing Robustness of Large Vision Language Models",
  "summary": "Both arXiv AI and arXiv Computer Vision reports present a dual adversarial fine-tuning framework that jointly optimizes visual and semantic supervision signals from two modalities, enhancing model robustness while generalizing across tasks. The proposed framework improves adversarial robustness by replacing the CLIP vision encoder in the original model, achieving cross-task robustness without retraining or architecture modifications.",
  "facts": [
